# =============================================================================
# ABNY — STAGING ENVIRONMENT, EVERY VARIABLE THE BACKEND ACTUALLY READS.
#
# This file is a CHECKLIST, not a file to copy onto a server. On Railway and
# on Render these values are set in the platform's own variable store; nothing
# with a real value in it is ever committed to this repository.
#
# NOT ONE VALUE BELOW IS INVENTED. Every entry is either
#
#   [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY]  — you create it, in your own account, and paste it.
#                             Where it can be generated locally, the exact
#                             command is given.
#   [SAFE DEFAULT]          — leave it as written, or leave it unset entirely;
#                             the stated behaviour is what you get.
#
# HOW THIS LIST WAS BUILT — by reading, not by memory:
#   * apps/backend/src/config/env.validation.ts        (the four hard requirements)
#   * apps/backend/src/config/application/secrets-validator.ts
#   * apps/backend/src/config/application/environment-validator.ts
#   * every `process.env.*` and `configService.get('...')` in apps/backend/src
# A variable that appears nowhere in those places does not appear here.
#
# FATAL vs WARNING is the backend's own vocabulary. A FATAL issue THROWS at
# boot and the process exits — the container will crash-loop and the platform
# will refuse the deployment, which is the correct outcome. A WARNING boots and
# degrades in the specific way its comment states.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. THE FOUR THE PROCESS WILL NOT START WITHOUT (FATAL)
#    env.validation.ts REQUIRED_ENV_VARS + SecretsValidator.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY] — from your own managed PostgreSQL.
# Must parse as a URL with scheme postgresql: or postgres: (EnvironmentValidator).
# On Railway paste the reference `${{Postgres.DATABASE_URL}}`; on Render this is
# wired by render.yaml's `fromDatabase` and you set nothing by hand.
# THE ROLE MATTERS: migration 0004 executes `CREATE ROLE abny_app` and GRANTs to
# it, so the user in this URL must be allowed to create a role. Railway's
# `postgres` user is; a restricted managed user may not be — see
# DEPLOY_STAGING.md §5 for what the failure looks like and what to do.
DATABASE_URL=

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY] — from your own managed Redis.
# Must parse as a URL with scheme redis: or rediss: (EnvironmentValidator).
# NOT optional: the throttler store, the scheduler's job leases and
# /health/ready all use it. On Railway paste `${{Redis.REDIS_URL}}`.
REDIS_URL=

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY] — generate, do not choose:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# At least 32 characters, and the two MUST be different values; both rules are
# FATAL in SecretsValidator. Staging's secrets must not equal production's —
# a token minted on staging must be worthless everywhere else.
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. SET THESE TOO — the backend boots without them and is wrong in a
#    specific, named way if you skip them (WARNING).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY] — 32-byte key, base64:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# LocationEvent lat/lng are encrypted with it before they are persisted.
# Missing: the backend boots and location-related features fail when used.
# CHANGING IT LATER MAKES EVERY ALREADY-ENCRYPTED ROW UNREADABLE. Generate it
# once per environment and keep it.
LOCATION_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY] — comma-separated origins, no trailing slash, no
# wildcard. main.ts defaults to an EMPTY array, which allows no browser origin
# at all: mis-setting this does not open a hole, it closes the dashboard out.
# Staging needs whichever origin the admin dashboard is served from, e.g. the
# Vite preview origin while you are testing from your own machine.
# Example shape (yours will differ): http://localhost:4173
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY] — generate:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# The shared secret for /admin/growth/*, /analytics/dashboard-metrics and
# GET /support. Unset, those endpoints fail CLOSED (deny everyone) — never
# open. It is sent as the `x-internal-admin-key` header.
# IT IS NOT A BUILD-TIME VARIABLE FOR THE DASHBOARD. The operator types it
# into the dashboard's unlock screen and it is held in memory only — never in
# localStorage, never in a cookie, never in a URL, never in the JS bundle.
# Staging's key must be a DIFFERENT value from production's.
INTERNAL_ADMIN_API_KEY=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. SAFE DEFAULTS — leave as-is unless you have a reason.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# [SAFE DEFAULT] Set by the image itself (ENV NODE_ENV=production). Listed so
# that seeing it in a dashboard variable list is not a surprise.
NODE_ENV=production

# [SAFE DEFAULT] Both Railway and Render inject PORT; main.ts falls back to
# 3000 when it is absent. Do not hardcode it unless your host requires it.
PORT=

# [SAFE DEFAULT] Leave UNSET. Container-local time is then UTC. The daily and
# per-category notification caps are computed from each family's own timezone
# (`Family.timezone`), not from the container's — setting TZ here changes
# nothing about them and only makes logs harder to compare.
TZ=

# [SAFE DEFAULT] Optional build stamp, surfaced by GET /api/v1/system/diagnostics.
# The deploy workflow can pass the commit SHA; empty is honest, not broken.
GIT_COMMIT_SHA=

# [SAFE DEFAULT] Leave unset (= off). When "true", AI rephrasing of
# notification copy is enabled. Off is the reviewed default for a pilot.
NOTIFICATION_AI_REPHRASE_ENABLED=

# [SAFE DEFAULT — WITH A CONSEQUENCE, READ IT] Where child-uploaded evidence
# (recitation audio, photos) is written. Defaults to `.evidence-store` inside
# the container, which is EPHEMERAL: on a container-based host every uploaded
# file disappears on the next deploy or restart. That is acceptable for
# staging and is NOT acceptable for a pilot with real families. Point it at a
# mounted volume before any real child data exists.
EVIDENCE_STORAGE_ROOT=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. OPTIONAL INTEGRATIONS — each degrades to a documented, safe no-op when
#    empty. Empty is a supported configuration; pretending otherwise is not.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY if you want real AI text] Without it, AI assistant,
# diagnostics and recommendation phrasing fall back to deterministic text.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# [SAFE DEFAULT] Must start with "claude-" or EnvironmentValidator warns.
AI_ASSISTANT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY if you want provider failover] The SECONDARY ring.
# With ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set and this empty, an Anthropic outage degrades every
# AI feature to deterministic text and fails /ai-assistant/ask outright.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY] Create a Sentry project in your own account and paste
# its DSN. Empty: errors are still logged locally by GlobalExceptionFilter,
# just not reported anywhere you can see them — which on staging is the
# difference between "we saw the crash" and "someone mentioned it".
SENTRY_DSN=

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY] The FULL Firebase service-account JSON, one line.
# Empty: PushNotificationService logs every send as a no-op. A push-delivery
# test on staging is meaningless until this is set.
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# [SAFE DEFAULT] Self-hosted analytics works without it.
POSTHOG_API_KEY=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. PAYMENTS — LEAVE EVERY ONE OF THESE EMPTY ON STAGING.
#
# Each adapter reports isConfigured() === false while its variables are blank,
# throws a typed 503 from anything that would call the provider, and returns
# {verified: false} — never true — from signature verification. An
# unconfigured deployment cannot be tricked into processing an unsigned
# callback, so empty is the SAFE state, not the incomplete one.
#
# Merchant onboarding (Paymob/Fawry, 4–8 weeks) is tracked in SHIP_BOARD.md as
# BLOCKED — HUMAN DECISION. The full meaning of every name below, and what the
# client must obtain for each, is in apps/backend/.env.example; it is not
# duplicated here so the two cannot drift.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
PAYMOB_API_KEY=
PAYMOB_HMAC_SECRET=
PAYMOB_INTEGRATION_ID=
PAYMOB_IFRAME_ID=
FAWRY_MERCHANT_CODE=
FAWRY_SECURITY_KEY=
FAWRY_BASE_URL=
MOYASAR_SECRET_KEY=
MOYASAR_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
MOYASAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
APPLE_ISSUER_ID=
APPLE_KEY_ID=
APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=
APPLE_BUNDLE_ID=
APPLE_USE_SANDBOX=false
APPLE_ROOT_CA_G3_FINGERPRINT=
GOOGLE_PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=
GOOGLE_PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY=
GOOGLE_PLAY_PACKAGE_NAME=
GOOGLE_PUBSUB_AUDIENCE=
GOOGLE_PUBSUB_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. THE ADMIN DASHBOARD — BUILD-TIME, and a different machine.
#
# The dashboard is a static bundle. Anything named VITE_* is inlined into that
# bundle and shipped to every visitor, so a secret can never be one.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY] The staging API base, INCLUDING the `/api/v1` prefix.
# Every route except /health/live and /health/ready is served under it.
# Example shape (yours will differ): https://<your-staging-host>/api/v1
VITE_API_BASE_URL=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. CI/CD NAMES — set in GitHub, not on the server.
#
# These are NOT application variables; the backend never reads them. They are
# listed here so that one file answers "what has to exist before a deploy",
# and `.github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml` asserts on every run that every
# name it uses appears in this file.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY] GitHub → Settings → Secrets → Actions.
# A Railway PROJECT token, scoped to the staging project. Never a personal
# account token: a project token cannot touch another project.
# RAILWAY_TOKEN

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY] GitHub → Settings → Variables → Actions.
# The exact Railway service name to deploy, as it appears in the project.
# RAILWAY_SERVICE_NAME

# [OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY] GitHub → Settings → Variables → Actions.
# The full URL of the staging liveness probe, e.g. https://<host>/health/live.
# The workflow curls it after deploying and fails the run if it is not 200.
# STAGING_HEALTH_URL
